{
  "schema": "bank-aliases/1",
  "notes": "Display name plus the spellings an OCR'd Indian complaint actually carries, keyed by IFSC bank code. The real RBI IFSC master carries one canonical bank spelling and no native-script rendering, so this table stays separate from ifsc_master_sample.json and survives a real-list drop-in. Aliases are matched with rapidfuzz; adding a spelling is a data change, never a code change. Point BANK_ALIASES_PATH at a replacement to override this file without editing the installed package.",
  "coverage_note": "Scheduled commercial banks (public sector, private, small finance, payments and the foreign banks that appear on Indian retail statements), the largest urban co-operative banks, and the pre-amalgamation names that still appear on documents predating the 2017-2020 mergers. Regional Rural Banks are NOT enumerated - there are more than forty and they are named after their sponsor bank and state, so an RRB complaint yields no bank_name rather than a wrong one. That is the intended failure: absence, never a neighbouring bank.",
  "non_party_note": "Institutions that appear on a complaint but are never the bank complained about. Every RB-IOS complaint is ADDRESSED to the Reserve Bank of India, and 'Bank of India' is a literal substring of 'Reserve Bank of India' - so without this list the addressee block of every letter yields a confident, wrong bank_name. Matched by the same longest-literal-wins rule as the bank aliases: when the longest exact match on a line is one of these, no bank is claimed for that span.",
  "non_party_institutions": [
    "Reserve Bank of India",
    "The Reserve Bank of India",
    "Reserve Bank",
